1. When datatype are not from custom object just String, Integer, Float
List<Integer> numbers = Arrays.asList(5, 3, 8, 1);
Optional<Integer> min = numbers.stream().min(Integer::compareTo);
System.out.println(min.get()); // Output: 1
Optional<Integer> max=numbers.stream().max(Integer::compareTo)
System.out.println(max.get()); // output 8

2. Finding max and min from custom objects fields
We need Comparator for custom objects fields

class Person {
    private String name;
    private int age;
    private double salary;
}
// Youngest person
Optional<Person> youngest = people.stream()
    .min(Comparator.comparingInt(Person::getAge));

// Oldest person
Optional<Person> oldest = people.stream()
    .max(Comparator.comparingInt(Person::getAge));

// Person with lowest salary
Optional<Person> lowestSalary = people.stream()
    .min(Comparator.comparingDouble(Person::getSalary));

// Person with highest salary
Optional<Person> highestSalary = people.stream()
    .max(Comparator.comparingDouble(Person::getSalary));

// First in alphabetical order
Optional<Person> firstAlphabetically = people.stream()
    .min(Comparator.comparing(Person::getName));

// Last in alphabetical order
Optional<Person> lastAlphabetically = people.stream()
    .max(Comparator.comparing(Person::getName));

// Find person with minimum age, and if ages are equal, minimum salary
Optional<Person> result = people.stream()
    .min(Comparator.comparingInt(Person::getAge)
                  .thenComparingDouble(Person::getSalary));
Note:
Use Comparator.comparing() for object fields
For specific variants for primitive fields use, comparingInt(),comparingDouble(),comparingLong()
The result is wrapped in Optional since the stream might be empty
Chain comparators with thenComparing() for secondary sorting criteria